ly for  us the author made that friend in the  military who fueled his work and love of  manwë if not for him we might have never  come to know bomb and the exciting world  of the tower for fact number two let's  look at bombs birthday bombs full name  is the 25th bomb and we're told that his  name comes from his birthday according  to bomb it was Rachel who actually told  him that his name comes from his  birthday so she seems to know  more than we do since for us Bob's  birthday is classified in fact the  author said that BOMs birthday is the  biggest secret interestingly enough BOM  was initially referred to by head-on as  and I quote the boy who was born on the  night that the tower cried and quote  however it was taken out in later  versions according to the author this  line is for shattering but he decided to  take it out because it might give too  much confusion in the beginning so we  only get some clue surrounding when BOM  was born but it's clearly gonna be a big  deal when we find out we don't know how  old BOM is but we do know that  characters in the Tower of God series  have much longer lifespans than we do  for instance waifu candidate yuri is at  least over 500 years old and there are  characters that are over a thousand  years old this is a unique twist that I  haven't come across often in the anime  I've seen so far for fact number three  let's look at BOMs height Bob's height  changes throughout the story as it  follows his physical and mental growth  his first recorded height is 168  centimeters or 5 feet and 6 inches and  later the author tells us that he  reaches around Koons height which is 181  centimeters or 5 feet and 11 inches thus  he at least becomes around 6 feet tall  and he might not be done growing yet  for instance Yuri is taller than you'd  expect an anime girl like her to be at  180 centimeters or also around 5 feet  and 11 inches tall and the author tells  us that within the tower Yuri is  actually on the smaller side so expect  to see a lot of huge characters as the  series progresses for fact number 4  let's look at BOMs name it has two  meanings in Korean it means night as in  the opposite of day and not the kind of  night who protects damsels in distress  in a suit of armor and bomb also means  chestnut a number of times characters  play on the chest on meaning of Baum's  name and call him tasty Knight also  makes sense with his name since he is  often associated with darkness he came  from a cave after all however it is also  in the night that stars shine and that's  also significant since Baum's been  compared to a shining star as well he  also gains another meaningful name later  on in the series but we won't go into  that here since the anime is  not that far along yet fact number five  bombs voice actor is the twenty  seven-year-old Taichi Ichikawa  from Tokyo Japan he's done more minor  roles in epic shows like men land saga  and JoJo's Bizarre Adventure and golden  wind but the protagonists of Tower of  God is definitely one of his bigger  roles he's made appearances in many  anime so far and I'm sure that we'll see  more of this young up-and-coming voice  actor in the following years and  according to behind the voice actors  calm it appears that the English dub is  going to be done by the veteran voice  actor Johnny Yong Bosch he's voiced many  iconic anime characters including the  loose from Code Geass and Ichigo from  Bleach for my fellow Demon Slayer fans  out there he also voiced the hilariously  antisocial water pillar gear for fact  number six let's talk about how Tower of  God was based on the Shonan genre and  how bomb compares and contrasts with the  conventional shown in hero Shonen is the  most popular demographic for manga  Shonen manga are primarily targeted at  males between the ages of 12 and 18 the  author of tower of god has said that  just as with other shortened  protagonists bomb will undergo internal  and external growth he will realize his  powers in advance farther as he climbs  the Tower of God but the author explains  unlike in Shonen bomb will not push his  Justice or friendship on others bombs  evolving powers won't be used for  something like that thus the author says  that the tower of God's story and  philosophy will be somewhere between  Shonen and seinen Satan is primarily  intended for an older demographic men  from their 20s to 50s just think about  the manga berserk and how you don't  expect to see guts going out of his way  to be friends with people although  powerful bomb is more withdrawn quiet  and unsure of himself and his beliefs  when compared to the average shown in  protagonist for fact number 7 let's talk  about bomb and his connection to jihad  the king of the tower jihad is the  figure that looms over the story even if  we don't see him much we know that he  has beautiful princesses associated with  him that can kick butt and that he's  probably the most powerful but he's  still surrounded in mystery bomb has  been noted to be similar to jihad in his  younger days jihad was also an irregular  the main difference between  - were told is that both sought power to  make people happy but bomb wanted power  so he could stay by the side of his  friends while king jihad wanted power so  that he could stand above others despite  this difference the author said that if  the two characters had met when jihad  was younger they would have gotten along  pretty well but as things stand they  have to have an antagonistic  relationship it's always interesting  when similarities are drawn between the  main character we're supposed to rule  for and the figure that seems to be at  this point at least the final  all-powerful boss of the series for fact  number 8 let's talk about bomb and  Rachel when asked if bomb and Rachel  were dating the author responded that  they aren't and that it's more  complicated than that according to the  author Rachel's not bombs love interest  but a female protagonist and even though  bomb seems like a simple  we're told that he'll be a heartbreaker  and make a lot of women cried before the  series is over fact number 9 bomb has  had multiple hairstyles throughout the  series from shorter hair to longer hair  that covers his eyes fans asked if bomb  would grow his hair long again in the  future and the author asked bomb kind of  how older asks his one-piece characters  questions and lets them respond in his  own question corner into one piece manga  volumes bomb responded that the long  hair is inconvenient so it looks like  it'll remain shorter for the most part  the author added that when he draws both  Koons hair and bombs hair he feels like  giving them a haircut but he knows that  for rock there isn't really anything to  cut fact number 10 as usual will be a  lightening round of sorts I guess we can  dub it the shin-soo round in this case  since we're dealing with hour of God all  lists as many facts about bomb as I can  in a relatively short period of time  three two one let's jam bombs Harry's  brown and his eyes are supposed to be  gold even though they kind of look  orange in the anime bomb is great at  cooking and his best dish is cream  spaghetti he doesn't eat salty stuff or  raw foods but he likes Korean food in  general bombs ambidextrous meaning they  can naturally use his left hand as well  as his right hand but he was still  taught to use his right hand more and  the author tells us that off-screen bomb  does a lot of training making it clear  that he works hard and is not just  expecting his talent to save him and  I definitely learned a lot of things  that I didn't know about bomb as I was  researching this video and I hope you  learned some new facts about him too if  you knew all this stuff then congrats  you are a tower of God stand of the  highest caliber if you did enjoy the  video and want to see more be sure to  smash that like button share this video  let me know what character you would  like to see next  if you